{
  "name": "Key Steps to a Barrier-Free Bathroom",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Creating a barrier-free bathroom is one of the most impactful home modifications you can make for safety and independence. Let's break down the key steps. First, you'll want to assess your current bathroom setup for any existing barriers. This includes doorways, shower entries, and vanity heights. Step two is identifying potential solutions. This often involves installing a curbless shower, which makes entry and exit super easy. You might also consider grab bars in the shower and near the toilet for added support – just make sure they have proper structural backing! Step three focuses on the vanity; an open knee-space vanity allows for comfortable access from a seated position. Step four is all about the flooring – non-slip options are essential to prevent falls. Finally, consider reachable controls for lighting and water. If you’re looking at structural changes or a complete layout redesign, calling in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC is a smart move. We can ensure everything is up to code and perfectly suited to your needs.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
